  deep: 'Mucilage sits between the pulp and the parchment and won\u2019t rinse off with water alone: it either ferments loose or dries onto the seed.[1] How much of it stays on while the coffee dries is the whole difference between washed, honey and natural.[2]',
  related: ['parchment', 'silverskin', 'washed', 'natural', 'honey', 'fermentation'],
  lesson: 'm1l7',
