  term: 'Silverskin',
  cat: 'beans',
  aliases: ['silverskin', 'silver skin', 'chaff'],
  "short": 'The tissue-thin membrane on a green bean. Most of it lifts off in the roaster as chaff.',
  deep: 'Silverskin is the last layer between parchment and seed. Roasting dries it and it flakes away as chaff, which roasters collect and discard \u2014 except in the centre crease, where a little usually stays behind. On naturals that trapped silverskin often looks stained.[1]',
