  aliases: ['centre cut', 'center cut', 'centre crease', 'center crease'],
  "short": 'The S-shaped crease down the flat face of a bean, where it was pressed against its twin inside the cherry.',
  deep: 'The centre cut is the first thing graders look at. It traps leftover silverskin, so it also records how the coffee was processed: pale and clean on a washed lot, often stained amber or reddish on a natural where fruit sugar dried in place.[1]',
