  term: 'Washed Process',
  cat: 'processing',
  aliases: ['washed process', 'washed'],
  "short": 'The fruit is stripped and the seeds are fermented and rinsed clean before drying \u2014 giving a clean, bright cup.',
  deep: 'Also called the \u201Cwet\u201D process. Removing the fruit early lets the bean\u2019s own character and acidity shine, with less of the fruit\u2019s influence. It needs plenty of water and careful fermentation control.[1] Washed Kenyans are the standard example: crisp, almost blackcurrant-like acidity.',
  related: ['natural', 'honey', 'fermentation'],
