  deep: 'Decaffeination is a processing step applied to green coffee, months before roasting. Solvent methods use ethyl acetate or methylene chloride; Swiss Water and CO\u2082 methods use none. All leave a few milligrams per cup \u2014 close to nothing, but not nothing.[1] A \u201Csugarcane decaf\u201D from Colombia was decaffeinated with ethyl acetate made from cane.',
