    explain: 'Acidity is a bright, structured quality with sweetness behind it; sourness is an empty, puckering taste that means the water never got enough out of the grounds. The test is whether anything else came with it \u2014 bright coffee tastes of fruit, sour coffee tastes of nothing much.'
