  "short": 'The texture and weight of coffee on your tongue \u2014 another word for body.',
  deep: 'Mouthfeel is what you feel rather than what you taste: the weight, the texture, how thick the coffee is. It comes from dissolved solids plus whatever oils and fine particles are still floating in the cup, so the filter you brew through changes it more than the coffee itself does.[1] Cuppers score it in its own section, separate from flavour.',
