  term: 'Finish',
  cat: 'sensory',
  aliases: ['finish', 'aftertaste'],
  "short": 'The flavour that lingers after you swallow \u2014 short and clean, or long and sweet.',
  deep: 'The finish \u2014 cuppers call it aftertaste \u2014 is what is left once you have swallowed: how long it lasts, and whether it stays pleasant. Good coffee fades away sweet and clean. Tired or badly brewed coffee turns papery, drying or ashy a few seconds later. It gets its own score because a cup can taste lovely at first and then fall apart.[1] Wait ten seconds after swallowing before judging it \u2014 the finish arrives late by definition.',
